# The decorator demo: a plain two-column pipe table, dressed on screen.
#
# The label column spends the TONE SLOT instead of naming a colour, so THIS FILE is
# the only copy that ever has to exist:
#   @{view:table}                 the default below, key
#   @{view:table, type:warning}   yellow, and the message still says what it is
#   @{view:table, tone:dim}       grey, a look with no semantics attached
# @tone declares what the slot holds when no decorator names a class.
@tone key
@fields rows label content
@each rows cap="1/3"
{{tone}}${label}{{/}}  ${content}
@end
